>
>It might even be a good idea to drop everything you're carrying if
>you're in a situation where you know you're about to die anyway.  I
>guess this doesn't work for armor.

This is a vague sort of cheating.  Not that cheating isn't fun
sometimes, of course.  If you're on a PC, not competing with others,
there's nothing wrong with it.  With that in mind, here's a more
direct way to accomplish this sort of cheating, on a PC.

You find something really good, like a potion of gain level.  You're
on Dlvl 5.  Go to Dlvl 4, drop the potion on the staircase, and go
back down to Dlvl5.  Now, shell out of the game with !, and make a
copy of LEVEL.4, the level file for dlvl 4 which has the potion in it.
Exit from the shell, you're back in NetHack, dlvl 5.  Go upstairs,
take the potion, then go right back down.  Now, shell out of the game
again, and copy the old level 4 file onto the new one.  Level 4 now
has the potion again, even though your character has it too.  Exit
from the shell, go upstairs, take the second potion.  You now have
two.

This seems like a lot of (un-fun) work to get one extra potion, but
not so.  Because now that you have two, you can repeat the process to
get four.  Then eight.  Then 16, and so on.

I haven't done this with 3.0 yet, so maybe it doesn't work anymore,
But I really don't see why it wouldn't.  Have fun!

